\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O for a closer walk with God,
\par A calm and heavenly frame,
\par A light to shine upon the road
\par That leads me to the Lamb.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Where is the blessedness I knew
\par When first I saw the Lord?
\par Where is that soul- refreshing view
\par Of Jesus and His word?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. What peaceful hours I once enjoyed!
\par How sweet their memory still!
\par But they have left an aching void
\par The world can never fill.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Return, O holy Dove! return,
\par Sweet messenger of rest!
\par I hate the sins that made  Thee mourn,
\par And drove Thee from my breast.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The dearest idol I have known,
\par Whate'er that idol be,
\par Help me to tear it from Thy throne,
\par And worship only Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. So shall my walk be close with God,
\par Calm and serene my frame;
\par So purer light shall mark the road
\par That leads me to the Lamb.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

